<title>USA: Bowne &amp; Co adopts shareholder rights plan.</title>
<headline>Bowne &amp; Co adopts shareholder rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bowne &amp; Co Inc said on Friday it adopted a shareholders rights plan for protection against &quot;coercive or unfair&quot; takeovers, but said it knows of no current acquisition effort.</p>
<p>Bowne declared a dividend of one preferred share purchase right for each outstanding share of its common stock. The rights entitle holders to buy one one-thousandth of a share of the company's newly designated Series B Junior Participating Preferred Stock at $125.</p>
<p>The rights do not become exercisable unless someone acquires 20 percent or more of Bowne's outstanding common shares.</p>
